<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Otto Wille Kuusinen</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1881">1881</a>–<a href="/years/1964">1964</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Otto Wille Kuusinen was a Finnish communist who fled to Soviet <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/finnish-civil-war">Finnish Civil War</a> of 1918 and became a leading figure of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/communist-international">Comintern</a>. During the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/winter-war">Winter War</a> of 1939 Stalin made him head of the puppet Finnish Democratic Republic at Terijoki. He then chaired the Supreme Soviet of the Karelo-Finnish SSR and later served in the Soviet Presidium.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/otto-wille-kuusinen.jpg" alt="Otto Wille Kuusinen" width="320" height="432" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Otto_Wille_Kuusinen.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
